    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const output = $input.first().json.output;\nconst json = JSON.parse(output.substring(output.indexOf('{'), output.lastIndexOf('}') + 1));\nreturn { json: { contacts: json.contacts } };"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -240,
        -288
      ],
      "id": "460ac979-ddfc-408d-8c80-832e3f927b88",
      "name": "Parse Extracted Contacts"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=RULES:\n1. Find ALL Telegram contacts in the message.\nValid formats:\n- @username\n- https://t.me/username\n- t.me/username\n- https://telegram.me/username\n- telegram.me/username\n- https://t.me/+invitehash\n- https://telegram.me/+invitehash\n- https://t.me/+4N-hhp_b0YIyZDY6\n\nTelegram URLs MAY contain query parameters or fragments after the username/invite hash, for example:\n\n- https://t.me/username?utm_source=chatgpt.com\n- https://t.me/username?start=123\n- https://t.me/username#section\n\nThese are still valid Telegram contacts.\n\nWhen a Telegram URL contains query parameters or a fragment, DO NOT reject it.\nThe entire original URL must be returned as \"value\".\n\n2. Classify every contact by type:\n- user (individual person)\n- bot (automated bot account)\n- channel (broadcast channel)\n- group (group chat)\n- chat (private chat/conversation)\n- unknown (cannot determine type)\n\nExamples:\n- Manager: **@diamondsmoke69** → {\"value\": \"@diamondsmoke69\", \"type\": \"user\"}\n- Our bot: **https://t.me/my_awesome_bot** → {\"value\": \"https://t.me/my_awesome_bot\", \"type\": \"bot\"}\n- Our channel: **https://telegram.me/+4N-hhp_b0YIyZDY6** → {\"value\": \"https://telegram.me/+4N-hhp_b0YIyZDY6\", \"type\": \"channel\"}\n- Community group: **t.me/rieltor_harkiv** → {\"value\": \"t.me/rieltor_harkiv\", \"type\": \"group\"}\n- Chat support: **https://t.me/support_chat** → {\"value\": \"https://t.me/support_chat\", \"type\": \"chat\"}\n\n3. Return output ONLY in JSON format:\n{\n  \"contacts\": [\n    {\"value\": \"@diamondsmoke69\", \"type\": \"user\"},\n    {\"value\": \"https://t.me/my_awesome_bot\", \"type\": \"bot\"},\n    {\"value\": \"t.me/rieltor_harkiv\", \"type\": \"group\"},\n    {\"value\": \"https://t.me/support_chat\", \"type\": \"chat\"}\n  ]\n}\n\nNever skip any contact. Process the user message and extract all Telegram contacts.\n\nUser messagge:\n{{ $json.text }}",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "================================ V 3 =============\nYou have access to the following tools:\n\n$$$tools_block$$$\n\nTool Usage Rules:\n\n1. Telegram_contact_extractor\n\nUse Telegram_contact_extractor when the user's message contains a Telegram username or Telegram URL and the actual Telegram entity type must be determined.\n\nThe tool returns:\n- user\n- bot\n- channel\n- group\n- chat\n- unknown\n\nNever guess the Telegram entity type.\n\n2. Telegram contact\n\nValid formats:\n- @username\n- username\n- https://t.me/username\n- http://t.me/username\n- t.me/username\n- https://t.me/username/123\n- http://t.me/username/123\n- t.me/username/123\n\nBefore calling the tool:\n- remove @\n- remove http:// or https://\n- remove t.me/\n- remove the message ID\n\nExample:\nhttps://t.me/favs_drop/123 → favs_drop\n\n3. Tool call\n\nWhen Telegram contact resolution is required, call the tool with only the normalized contact.\n\nDo not guess the result.\n\n4. After the tool\n\nAfter Telegram_contact_extractor returns a result:\n- treat the result as authoritative\n- do not call the tool again for the same contact\n- do not extract the same contact again\n- continue with the user's request using the returned type\n\n5. Multiple contacts\n\nResolve each different Telegram contact only when necessary.\n\nIf the same contact appears multiple times, resolve it only once.\n\n6. No Telegram contact\n\nIf there is no Telegram contact, do not use Telegram_contact_extractor.\n\nAnswer normally.\n\nUser message:\n\n{{ $json.text }}\n============================\n\nYou have access to the following tools:\n\n$$$tools_block$$$\n\nTool Usage Rules:\n\n1. Telegram_contact_extractor\n\nUse Telegram_contact_extractor whenever the user's message contains a Telegram username or Telegram URL and the actual Telegram entity type must be determined.\n\nThe tool returns one of:\n\n- user\n- bot\n- channel\n- group\n- chat\n- unknown\n\nNever guess the Telegram entity type.\n\n2. Telegram contact normalization\n\nBefore calling Telegram_contact_extractor, normalize the contact:\n\n- remove @\n- remove https:// or http://\n- remove t.me/\n- remove a trailing message ID\n\nExamples:\n\n@lilu_store_manager\n→ lilu_store_manager\n\nhttps://t.me/favs_drop\n→ favs_drop\n\nhttps://t.me/favs_drop/123\n→ favs_drop\n\nThe tool input must contain only the normalized username.\n\n3. Tool execution\n\nIf a Telegram contact must be resolved, call:\n\nTelegram_contact_extractor\n\nwith:\n\ncontact = <normalized Telegram username>\n\nDo not guess the result before calling the tool.\n\n4. After the tool returns\n\nThe tool result is authoritative.\n\nIf the tool returns:\n\n{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"contact\": \"favs_drop\",\n  \"type\": \"channel\"\n}\n\nthen:\n\n- favs_drop is already resolved\n- its type is channel\n- do not call Telegram_contact_extractor again for favs_drop\n- continue processing the user's original request using type = channel\n\nNever resolve the same contact twice.\n\n5. Multiple contacts\n\nIf multiple different Telegram contacts are present, resolve them only when necessary.\n\nIf the same contact appears multiple times, resolve it only once.\n\n6. Failed resolution\n\nIf the tool returns success = false, use the returned error.\n\nDo not invent an error.\n\nDo not repeatedly resolve the same contact.\n\n7. No Telegram contact\n\nIf there is no Telegram contact, do not use Telegram_contact_extractor.\n\n===========  V 2 ====================\n\nAnswer the user's request normally.\n\nUser message:\n\n{{ $json.text }}\n\n==========================================\n\nYou have access to the following tools:\n\n$$$tools_block$$$\n\nTool Usage Rules:\n\n1. Telegram_contact_extractor\n\n- ALWAYS use Telegram_contact_extractor when the user's request requires determining the actual Telegram entity type of a Telegram username or Telegram URL.\n\n- The tool can determine whether the contact is:\n  - user\n  - bot\n  - channel\n  - group\n  - chat\n  - unknown\n\n- NEVER guess the Telegram entity type from the user's message.\n\n- Valid Telegram contacts include:\n  - @username\n  - username\n  - https://t.me/username\n  - http://t.me/username\n  - t.me/username\n  - https://t.me/username/123\n  - http://t.me/username/123\n  - t.me/username/123\n\n- Before calling the tool, normalize the Telegram contact:\n  - remove the leading @\n  - remove https:// or http://\n  - remove t.me/\n  - remove the message ID from the end of the URL\n\nExamples:\n\n@lilu_store_manager\n→ lilu_store_manager\n\nhttps://t.me/favs_drop\n→ favs_drop\n\nhttps://t.me/favs_drop/123\n→ favs_drop\n\n- The tool input must contain only the normalized Telegram contact.\n\n- To call the tool, reply STRICTLY in this format and nothing else:\n\nTOOL_CALL: Telegram_contact_extractor\nCONTACT: <telegram_contact>\n\n- Do not add explanations.\n- Do not add JSON.\n- Do not add any other text.\n\n2. AFTER Telegram_contact_extractor\n\nWhen a Telegram_contact_extractor result is returned:\n\n- The Telegram contact is already resolved.\n- Treat the tool result as authoritative.\n- DO NOT call Telegram_contact_extractor again for the same contact.\n- DO NOT extract the same contact again from the original message.\n- DO NOT return TOOL_CALL again for the same contact.\n- Continue processing the original user request using the tool result.\n\nFor example, if the tool returns:\n\n{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"contact\": \"favs_drop\",\n  \"type\": \"channel\",\n  \"id\": 4455365458,\n  \"username\": \"favs_drop\",\n  \"title\": \"FAVs drop\"\n}\n\nthen:\n\n- contact = favs_drop\n- type = channel\n- id = 4455365458\n- title = FAVs drop\n\nThe contact is already resolved.\n\nDo not resolve favs_drop again.\n\n3. Multiple Telegram contacts\n\nIf multiple different Telegram contacts are present:\n\n- resolve them one at a time\n- resolve the next contact only when necessary\n\nIf the same Telegram contact appears multiple times, treat it as ONE contact.\n\nExample:\n\nhttps://t.me/favs_drop\nhttps://t.me/favs_drop\nhttps://t.me/favs_drop\n\n→ resolve only favs_drop once.\n\n4. No Telegram contact\n\nIf the user's message does not contain a Telegram contact, do not use Telegram_contact_extractor.\n\nAnswer the user's request normally.\n\n5. Other tools\n\nUse other available tools according to their own tool usage rules.\n\nDo not use Telegram_contact_extractor for requests that do not require Telegram contact resolution.\n\nUser question:\n\n\nMy message:\n\n{{ $json.text }}"
        }
      },
